SimpleThreads Read MeThis sample demonstrates a simple use of cooperative threads.  It is based on the Macrame and Spinaker Pink sample apps originally by Art Cabral.  This sample uses the Threading suite as well as MacApp release 13.Features to note:Cooperative thread yielding is provided by the TThreadingIdler class, an idle cohandler that can be customized to provide appropriate yield behavior for a particular application.Each view has its own independent drawing thread.  Frequent yielding is required to provide the appearance of smooth, asynchronous, behavior.  Global states must be resynchronized after each yield.Views synchronize their destruction with the termination of their drawing thread.  This is required to prevent the thread from attempting to access a deleted view.Limitations:Only cooperative, Thread Manager threads are demonstrated by this sample.  A separate sample to demonstrate Multiprocessor tasks is under development.The threading library is currently built to support both cooperative and MP threading on Power PC, so both ThreadsLib and the Multiprocessing API Library are required for PPC builds.  Conditional compilation will be added before the final release.Due to a dependency on the Standard Template Library, only Code Warrior support is provided at this time.  The projects in this package are vanilla Code Warrior 10.Other notes:Code Warrior's resolution of the path for DragLib is ambiguous, which can lead to errors after a project is modified.  If you get an error for DragLib, remove the file from the project and reinsert the statically linked library from the Mac OS Support folder in Code Warrior.Steven McGrathOctober 13, 1996